## Project Structure

Rails Way first: follow the conventional layout and extract objects only when a model or controller grows.

```
{{PROJECT_NAME}}/
├── app/
│   ├── controllers/              # Thin, RESTful controllers
│   │   └── concerns/
│   ├── models/                   # Active Record models, validations, scopes
│   │   └── concerns/
│   ├── views/                    # ERB templates, Turbo Streams
│   ├── helpers/
│   ├── javascript/               # Stimulus controllers (importmap or bundler)
│   │   └── controllers/
│   ├── jobs/                     # Active Job classes (Solid Queue)
│   ├── mailers/
│   ├── channels/                 # Action Cable (Solid Cable)
│   ├── services/                 # Service objects (extracted on demand)
│   ├── queries/                  # Query objects (extracted on demand)
│   ├── forms/                    # Form objects (extracted on demand)
│   └── policies/                 # Authorization (Pundit, if used)
│
├── config/
│   ├── routes.rb
│   ├── database.yml
│   ├── credentials.yml.enc       # Encrypted credentials
│   ├── deploy.yml                # Kamal configuration
│   ├── ci.rb                     # bin/ci steps (Rails 8.1)
│   ├── initializers/
│   └── environments/
│
├── db/
│   ├── migrate/
│   ├── schema.rb
│   └── seeds.rb
│
├── lib/                          # Framework-independent code, rake tasks
├── spec/ or test/                # RSpec or Minitest
│   ├── models/
│   ├── requests/                 # (test/integration for Minitest)
│   ├── system/                   # Capybara system tests
│   ├── services/
│   ├── jobs/
│   ├── factories/                # FactoryBot (or test/fixtures)
│   └── support/
│
├── bin/                          # rails, setup, ci, rubocop, brakeman, dev
├── docker/                       # Docker configuration
├── docs/                         # Documentation and ADRs
├── Gemfile
├── Gemfile.lock
├── .ruby-version
└── .rubocop.yml
```

